WEBVTT

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.063
The Kol-Ut-Shan...

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:37.968
a cornerstone of our beliefs.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:41.302
Infinite diversity
in infinite combinations.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:44.571
I know all about
Vulcan philosophies.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.373
Why have you come here?

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.142
I was sent against my will.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.116
Then I suggest you leave.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.982
I'm not a prisoner?

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.544
Only of your emotions

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.318
or so I have been told.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.825
My emotions free me.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.794
I see.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:06.923
It's regrettable that I won't
be able to teach you.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.093
Where should I go?

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.660
Are you seeking my counsel?

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:15.538
I... can't return home.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.940
My father has banished me.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.444
Your school?

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.945
They revoked my seat.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.811
Why?

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.942
Because I refuse
to deny myself passion,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:29.386
the way you
and men like my father do.

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.321
You reject logic?

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.325
If I was meant
to deny feelings,

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.293
why was I born with them?

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.988
Where's the logic in that?

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:41.465
Hidden for you to find...

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:45.368
or in plain sight
for you to ignore.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.838
You speak in riddles
because the truth frightens you.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:48.839
You're right.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.569
It does frighten me.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.838
You are surprised

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:56.814
to hear a Vulcan master admit
to having emotions?

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.316
Yes.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.376
Emotions can be
a powerful tool.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.321
To deny their existence
is illogical,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.689
but you must learn
to control them.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.523
Why?

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.227
Do you wish to be taught?

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.530
I would question
everything you say.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:23.337
You would not be
a worthy pupil otherwise.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.275
Let us begin.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.780
Sit down, Tuvok.

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:54.071
Tun beveg!

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:55.079
Uh, sorry?

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:58.447
Senn... nebah senn?

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:01.919
Either the universal
translator's off-line

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:04.081
or I hit my head
harder than I thought.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.215
Ruck.

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.223
All right.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.259
Take it easy.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.057
All right, all right.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.255
Take it easy.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.388
Fitah!

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:15.696
This?

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.531
Listen, I really need this.

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:18.763
Fitah! Ud neetot!

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.601
Okay, okay.

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:43.195
First day in town
and I've already been mugged.

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:14.989
Ah.

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:59.528
I'm Commander Tuvok
of the Starship Voyager.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:04.771
Tuvok.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:07.645
Tuvok.

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:10.181
Yes.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:11.443
And you?

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:13.951
Noss.

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:16.215
Noss.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:31.265
We'll go to my vessel.

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:41.212
I see you've already been there.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:44.777
Mayday, Mayday.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.648
Paris to Voyager.
Respond.

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:49.880
Aw, come on.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.057
Her name is Noss.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.323
She was attacked
by two humanoid males.

00:09:59.565 --> 00:10:01.658
You sure she didn't attack them?

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:03.599
They were attempting
to rob her.

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:06.399
Seems to be a local pastime.

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:25.791
She requires medical attention.

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:29.954
I'd love to help,
but somebody stole our medkits.

00:10:38.404 --> 00:10:39.871
Food.

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:45.505
What's the status
of the shuttle?

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:47.546
Fractures throughout the hull,

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:49.513
environmental systems down,

00:10:49.582 --> 00:10:52.517
impulse engines
are beyond repair.

00:10:52.585 --> 00:10:55.383
Told you we should have
brought the Delta Flyer.

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:59.121
Communications appear
to be functional.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:01.125
Won't do us any good.

00:11:01.193 --> 00:11:02.785
Every time
I transmit a signal,

00:11:02.862 --> 00:11:05.194
it gets bounced back
by the distortion field

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:06.663
that pulled us down here.

00:11:08.868 --> 00:11:12.304
It looks like we fell into
some kind of gravity well.

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:13.929
As far as I can tell,

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:16.804
this planet is a part
of an entire solar system

00:11:16.876 --> 00:11:19.208
that is stuck
in a pocket of subspace.

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:20.472
Fascinating.

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:22.741
Yeah.

00:11:22.815 --> 00:11:24.339
Well, scientific
interest aside,

00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.180
I don't see any
easy way out of here.

00:11:26.252 --> 00:11:28.948
No doubt Voyager
has begun a rescue effort.

00:11:29.055 --> 00:11:30.249
The Doctor?

00:11:30.322 --> 00:11:32.119
His mobile emitter was
damaged during the crash.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:33.488
With a little luck,
I might be able

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:35.083
to repair it and bring
him back on line.

00:11:35.161 --> 00:11:37.095
Make it your top priority.

00:11:37.163 --> 00:11:38.824
Gren, gren.

00:11:38.898 --> 00:11:40.559
What is it?

00:11:41.901 --> 00:11:44.062
13 humanoids approaching...

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:46.604
the same species
that attacked her.

00:11:46.672 --> 00:11:48.833
Gather as many supplies
as you can carry.

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:50.170
We're leaving.

00:11:50.242 --> 00:11:52.335
You really think it's smart
to abandon the shuttle?

00:11:52.411 --> 00:11:54.675
Noss appears to have survived
here for some time.

00:11:54.747 --> 00:11:56.180
It's logical to assume

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:58.113
she has access
to a more secure shelter.

00:11:58.184 --> 00:12:00.118
Nemmok. Eilen.

00:12:00.186 --> 00:12:01.778
Eilen.

00:12:01.854 --> 00:12:04.345
Whatever you say.

00:12:32.151 --> 00:12:34.176
Eid kahn.

00:13:10.189 --> 00:13:13.352
Doesn't look like this bird's
going to fly, either.

00:13:13.425 --> 00:13:15.586
Minimal power
and life-support,

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:18.687
but the ship is protected
by a force field.

00:13:18.764 --> 00:13:21.927
That explains how
she's been able to survive here.

00:13:22.034 --> 00:13:23.934
Anything resembling
an engine?

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:26.904
I'm detecting engine debris
two kilometers away.

00:13:26.972 --> 00:13:29.770
It is of the same
configuration as this vessel.

00:13:29.842 --> 00:13:31.309
Great.

00:13:31.377 --> 00:13:33.641
We've got two unusable ships,
and the only way

00:13:33.712 --> 00:13:36.078
Voyager is going
to detect our distress call

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:38.275
is if they crash-land
right on top of us.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.942
Progress?

00:13:40.019 --> 00:13:43.887
The optronic relays
took heavy damage.

00:13:43.956 --> 00:13:47.722
I'm bypassing
the primary circuits.

00:13:47.793 --> 00:13:49.226
Come on, Doc.

00:13:49.295 --> 00:13:51.855
I know you're in there.

00:13:55.234 --> 00:13:56.826
I'm guessing we hit a snag.

00:13:56.902 --> 00:13:58.426
An accurate assumption.

00:14:01.407 --> 00:14:02.465
Rev din ud?

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:04.639
Ud rev?

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.143
Tun sang.

00:14:06.212 --> 00:14:08.339
Ton rev ud tim seid.

00:14:09.715 --> 00:14:11.376
You speak her language?

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:15.352
A universal translator
was written into my program.

00:14:15.421 --> 00:14:17.514
Ask her how long
she's been here,

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.750
if she knows a way

00:14:18.824 --> 00:14:21.019
to get back through
that sinkhole.

00:14:21.093 --> 00:14:25.086
Din yee ton ud lurka?

00:14:25.164 --> 00:14:28.622
Pah din nefta menruk?

00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:30.225
Lurka heen.

00:14:30.302 --> 00:14:33.032
Zin ik lurka

00:14:33.105 --> 00:14:35.300
ud ruck totta.

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:38.343
Mah'ees bin ruck ayah.

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:41.208
What'd she say?

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:45.649
She said she's been here
14 seasons

00:14:45.718 --> 00:14:48.778
and in that time, she's seen
many ships come down,

00:14:48.854 --> 00:14:51.516
but she's never seen one
go back up again.

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.520
Come back,
you little bloodsucker.

00:15:23.989 --> 00:15:25.286
I don't know what's worse...

00:15:25.357 --> 00:15:26.881
catching them or eating them.

00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:28.324
No poison.

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:30.089
Well, they may not
be poisonous,

00:15:30.162 --> 00:15:32.096
but they give me the creeps.

00:15:32.164 --> 00:15:34.724
Maybe I should have
left the hunting

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:35.767
to you and Tuvok.

00:15:35.834 --> 00:15:37.028
Let me.

00:15:53.319 --> 00:15:56.220
Looks delicious.

00:16:03.996 --> 00:16:05.657
Shut down my program?

00:16:05.731 --> 00:16:06.993
Why?

00:16:07.066 --> 00:16:08.693
Our resources are
severely limited.

00:16:08.767 --> 00:16:10.860
We may need your mobile emitter
as a source of power.

00:16:10.936 --> 00:16:12.597
I'm a Doctor, not a battery.

00:16:12.671 --> 00:16:13.638
Until we're rescued

00:16:13.706 --> 00:16:15.196
or you're needed
for an emergency,

00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:17.333
I must insist
that you remain off-line.

00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:20.139
Make way for the mighty hunters.

00:16:20.212 --> 00:16:24.239
If Mr. Paris' hunting ability
is any indication,

00:16:24.316 --> 00:16:26.045
maybe we should
take him off-line.

00:16:26.118 --> 00:16:28.643
Thanks for the vote
of confidence, Doc.

00:16:28.721 --> 00:16:30.086
The hunt was good.

00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:34.182
Impressive.

00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:37.625
Voyager has 15 decks,

00:16:37.696 --> 00:16:39.163
a crew of 152,

00:16:39.231 --> 00:16:41.893
warp and impulse engines.

00:16:41.967 --> 00:16:44.435
I want to see.

00:16:44.503 --> 00:16:46.232
Someday, perhaps.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.802
Tell me about you there.

00:16:50.876 --> 00:16:53.003
I am the Chief Tactical Officer.

00:16:55.681 --> 00:16:57.876
What else?

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.475
Can you be more specific?

00:17:00.552 --> 00:17:03.715
Your duties, uh...

00:17:03.789 --> 00:17:06.622
Where you sleep?

00:17:06.692 --> 00:17:08.216
What you eat?

00:17:08.293 --> 00:17:09.885
Music?

00:17:09.962 --> 00:17:11.293
Friends?

00:17:11.363 --> 00:17:13.797
Why is any of that relevant?

00:17:15.134 --> 00:17:17.602
Because it is you.

00:17:20.873 --> 00:17:24.365
When I first met her,
she wouldn't even look at me,

00:17:24.443 --> 00:17:27.537
but she warmed up after,
oh... three years.

00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:30.673
The longest flirtation
in Starfleet history.

00:17:30.749 --> 00:17:32.808
No kidding.

00:17:32.885 --> 00:17:36.252
She sounds... fascinating.

00:17:36.321 --> 00:17:38.516
I just hope I see her again.

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:40.558
You must really...

00:17:44.029 --> 00:17:45.826
bot yah jouton.

00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:49.361
Love her very much.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.365
Yeah.

00:17:58.844 --> 00:18:01.278
More spiders?

00:18:01.346 --> 00:18:03.439
Oh, no, thank you.

00:18:03.515 --> 00:18:05.608
Three's my limit.

00:18:05.684 --> 00:18:07.174
I will assist you.

00:18:10.656 --> 00:18:14.752
Well, I suppose it's time
I shut down my program.

00:18:14.827 --> 00:18:16.624
Good night, Doc.

00:18:34.646 --> 00:18:36.307
She likes you.

00:18:36.381 --> 00:18:38.906
She has been alone
for many years.

00:18:39.051 --> 00:18:41.212
She appreciates our company.

00:18:42.688 --> 00:18:47.318
No. I mean...
she likes you.

00:18:48.393 --> 00:18:50.156
What are you implying?

00:18:50.229 --> 00:18:51.457
Oh, come on, Tuvok.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.055
You may be cold,
but you're not blind.

00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:57.364
Need I remind you
that I am married?

00:18:57.436 --> 00:18:59.870
Your wife is
50,000 light-years away

00:18:59.938 --> 00:19:01.565
in a different layer of space.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.870
The chances of you ever
seeing her again

00:19:03.942 --> 00:19:05.500
are practically nonexistent.

00:19:07.446 --> 00:19:08.845
Excuse me.

00:19:21.693 --> 00:19:24.218
What are you doing?

00:19:24.296 --> 00:19:26.560
I'm recalibrating
the distress beacon.

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:29.833
Listen, um...

00:19:29.902 --> 00:19:33.565
what I said in there
about your wife...

00:19:33.639 --> 00:19:35.106
I'm sorry.

00:19:35.174 --> 00:19:37.301
I didn't mean
to hurt your feelings.

00:19:37.376 --> 00:19:39.310
I have no feelings
for you to hurt.

00:19:42.247 --> 00:19:43.646
I think you do.

00:19:43.715 --> 00:19:46.081
You work hard to bury them,

00:19:46.151 --> 00:19:47.914
but they're there.

00:19:50.556 --> 00:19:52.922
And even if they're not,

00:19:52.991 --> 00:19:56.358
this is home now.

00:19:56.428 --> 00:19:58.919
You might as well accept it
and try to find

00:19:58.997 --> 00:20:00.396
as much happiness as you can.

00:20:02.734 --> 00:20:04.326
Listen, you have a chance

00:20:04.403 --> 00:20:07.065
to make a decent life
for yourself here.

00:20:07.139 --> 00:20:10.404
There is still a possibility
that Voyager will rescue us.

00:20:10.475 --> 00:20:12.602
You may see
Lieutenant Torres again.

00:20:12.678 --> 00:20:14.771
If I didn't know you better,

00:20:14.846 --> 00:20:18.577
I'd say you were trying
to cheer me up, Tuvok.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.175
Is there a point
to your pessimism?

00:20:21.253 --> 00:20:22.379
It's not pessimism.

00:20:22.454 --> 00:20:23.546
It's practicality.

00:20:23.622 --> 00:20:26.113
You of all people
should understand that.

00:20:28.393 --> 00:20:30.224
Look, I've never
met your wife,

00:20:30.295 --> 00:20:32.695
but if she's half
as logical as you are,

00:20:32.764 --> 00:20:35.289
I bet you she'd tell
you the same thing.

00:20:37.769 --> 00:20:40.602
Your attempt to play
matchmaker is misguided.

00:20:40.672 --> 00:20:42.640
I am not experiencing
Pon farr.

00:20:42.708 --> 00:20:44.300
What difference does it make?

00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:46.173
You obviously care about Noss.

00:20:46.245 --> 00:20:49.476
If you won't admit it to me,
at least admit it to yourself.

00:20:49.548 --> 00:20:53.211
I respect her ability
to survive.

00:20:53.285 --> 00:20:54.980
It's more than that.

00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:57.988
I've seen the way
you look at her.

00:20:58.056 --> 00:20:59.353
What way is that?

00:21:00.659 --> 00:21:04.060
Like someone who wishes
he wasn't Vulcan.

00:21:14.139 --> 00:21:15.572
I'm sorry I was born Vulcan.

00:21:15.641 --> 00:21:17.802
B'Elak paar.

00:21:17.876 --> 00:21:20.140
Self-pity.

00:21:20.212 --> 00:21:22.612
Are you cataloging
my emotions?

00:21:22.681 --> 00:21:24.740
What is the source
of your self-pity?

00:21:24.816 --> 00:21:25.908
Isn't it obvious?

00:21:25.984 --> 00:21:28.282
If I weren't Vulcan,
I wouldn't be here now,

00:21:28.353 --> 00:21:30.378
going through
this pointless ritual.

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:33.322
You see only what
is in front of you.

00:21:33.392 --> 00:21:35.952
You must learn
to see behind you.

00:21:36.028 --> 00:21:37.154
Another riddle.

00:21:37.229 --> 00:21:39.493
I have no eyes to see behind me.

00:21:39.564 --> 00:21:41.555
You have the eyes of memory,

00:21:41.633 --> 00:21:43.965
the knowledge
of why you are here

00:21:44.102 --> 00:21:46.332
and why you have lost control.

00:21:51.076 --> 00:21:52.600
Tell me your story.

00:21:53.679 --> 00:21:55.738
My father's
already explained it.

00:21:55.814 --> 00:21:58.510
I wish to hear it from you.

00:22:02.354 --> 00:22:03.844
Her name is Jara.

00:22:03.922 --> 00:22:06.789
Her father's
a Terrelian diplomat.

00:22:06.858 --> 00:22:09.520
She's been granted
a seat at my school.

00:22:09.594 --> 00:22:11.118
And you have developed

00:22:11.196 --> 00:22:13.562
an emotional attraction
toward her.

00:22:13.632 --> 00:22:15.395
Yes.

00:22:15.467 --> 00:22:16.729
You love her.

00:22:16.802 --> 00:22:18.064
Yes.

00:22:18.136 --> 00:22:20.001
Does she love you?

00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:24.138
No. She's...

00:22:26.078 --> 00:22:30.777
Jara... doesn't return
my feelings.

00:22:30.849 --> 00:22:34.785
What if I were to say
that I received a letter

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:38.880
from your father telling me
that Jara is in love

00:22:38.957 --> 00:22:41.187
with one
of your fellow students?

00:22:41.259 --> 00:22:42.385
That's a lie!

00:22:43.729 --> 00:22:45.094
Who is it?

00:22:45.163 --> 00:22:46.790
Jealousy?

00:22:46.865 --> 00:22:48.389
I'll challenge him.

00:22:48.467 --> 00:22:50.458
That would be illogical,

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:53.766
because I have received
no such letter.

00:22:55.807 --> 00:22:57.968
You're trying to trick me.

00:22:58.110 --> 00:23:01.637
No. I'm trying to help
you to understand.

00:23:01.713 --> 00:23:03.806
Shon-ha'lock... love...

00:23:03.882 --> 00:23:06.908
is the most dangerous
emotion of all.

00:23:07.052 --> 00:23:09.816
It produces
many other emotions...

00:23:09.888 --> 00:23:14.348
jealousy, shame, rage, grief.

00:23:14.426 --> 00:23:17.623
You must learn
to suppress them all.

00:23:17.696 --> 00:23:20.665
Otherwise, they will
consume you.

00:23:23.201 --> 00:23:27.365
I can sense emotions
building inside you

00:23:27.439 --> 00:23:29.873
like a gathering storm.

00:23:29.941 --> 00:23:34.844
If we begin now,
we may be able to stop them.

00:23:43.655 --> 00:23:45.555
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:23:45.624 --> 00:23:47.114
It's been over an hour

00:23:47.192 --> 00:23:50.161
since the shuttle
disappeared from sensors.

00:23:50.228 --> 00:23:52.594
I'm not detecting any debris.

00:23:52.664 --> 00:23:55.258
Maybe the shuttle was tractored
or transported somewhere.

00:23:55.333 --> 00:23:56.322
Scan the region.

00:23:56.401 --> 00:23:58.562
Look for plasma emissions
or EM displacements...

00:23:58.637 --> 00:24:00.468
anything that might
indicate another ship.

00:24:00.539 --> 00:24:01.801
Nothing out of the ordinary...

00:24:01.873 --> 00:24:03.340
hydrogen, helium, space dust.

00:24:03.408 --> 00:24:04.568
There has to be
something out there.

00:24:04.643 --> 00:24:07.203
Shuttles don't just vanish
into thin air.

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:10.180
It's a gravimetric shear.

00:24:10.248 --> 00:24:11.180
Source?

00:24:11.249 --> 00:24:12.181
Unknown.

00:24:12.250 --> 00:24:13.182
Red Alert.

00:24:13.251 --> 00:24:15.151
Helm, full ahead.

00:24:21.726 --> 00:24:24.559
We're caught in some kind
of subspace sinkhole.

00:24:24.629 --> 00:24:26.062
It's pulling us in.

00:24:27.132 --> 00:24:29.225
The gravimetric shear's
increasing.

00:24:29.301 --> 00:24:30.233
Go to warp.

00:24:30.302 --> 00:24:32.361
I can't establish
a stable field.

00:24:32.437 --> 00:24:34.803
Then we need more power
to the impulse engines.

00:24:34.873 --> 00:24:35.931
That won't be enough.

00:24:36.074 --> 00:24:37.939
We've got to find a way to
counter the gravitational pull.

00:24:38.043 --> 00:24:39.135
B'Elanna, vent

00:24:39.211 --> 00:24:40.940
three million isodynes of plasma
from the nacelles.

00:24:41.012 --> 00:24:43.344
Chakotay, reverse
shield polarity.

00:24:49.688 --> 00:24:50.712
We're clear.

00:24:50.789 --> 00:24:51.756
Move us away.

00:24:51.823 --> 00:24:53.347
Stand down Red Alert.

00:24:53.425 --> 00:24:55.017
Secure all stations.

00:24:57.095 --> 00:24:59.120
I'd say we have
a pretty good idea

00:24:59.197 --> 00:25:00.960
what happened to that shuttle.

00:25:01.099 --> 00:25:04.830
The anomaly is approximately
600 meters in diameter.

00:25:04.903 --> 00:25:06.632
It's out of phase
with normal space.

00:25:06.705 --> 00:25:08.502
Even after recalibrating
the sensors,

00:25:08.573 --> 00:25:09.835
it barely registers.

00:25:09.908 --> 00:25:13.435
The distortion circumscribes
a subspace zone that includes

00:25:13.512 --> 00:25:15.241
a type-G sun and three planets.

00:25:15.313 --> 00:25:17.440
Any sign of the shuttle?

00:25:17.516 --> 00:25:19.347
No.

00:25:19.417 --> 00:25:21.908
I'd say it's time to break out
the multispatial probe.

00:25:22.020 --> 00:25:23.578
Agreed.

00:25:23.655 --> 00:25:25.213
What the hell is that?

00:25:25.290 --> 00:25:27.884
A vessel approaching
off the port bow.

00:25:27.959 --> 00:25:29.927
They've locked on
a tractor beam.

00:25:29.995 --> 00:25:32.225
Captain to the Bridge.

00:25:36.334 --> 00:25:38.495
I'm only going
to say this one more time.

00:25:38.570 --> 00:25:40.231
Disengage
your tractor beam, sir.

00:25:40.305 --> 00:25:42.933
You were in danger
of being pulled

00:25:43.008 --> 00:25:44.669
into the distortion.

00:25:44.743 --> 00:25:47.473
You should show
a little gratitude.

00:25:47.546 --> 00:25:50.379
We appreciate your help,
but we didn't ask for...

00:25:52.951 --> 00:25:55.715
Captain, this is Mr. Yost.

00:25:55.787 --> 00:26:00.588
Supervisor Yost,
Renovation Team Nova.

00:26:00.659 --> 00:26:03.594
Captain Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:26:03.662 --> 00:26:05.994
Until tomorrow,
I suggest you stay

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:09.659
at least two million kilometers
from the distortion.

00:26:09.734 --> 00:26:11.133
What happens tomorrow?

00:26:11.202 --> 00:26:13.762
The rift will be closed by then.

00:26:13.838 --> 00:26:16.329
Some of our crew
are trapped inside.

00:26:16.408 --> 00:26:17.602
I am sorry.

00:26:17.676 --> 00:26:21.908
We have lost 11 ships
to the distortion

00:26:22.013 --> 00:26:23.446
over the last year.

00:26:23.515 --> 00:26:24.914
It must be sealed.

00:26:25.016 --> 00:26:27.143
What about your people?

00:26:27.218 --> 00:26:30.779
Even if there were survivors,
there's no way to rescue them.

00:26:30.855 --> 00:26:32.413
The best we can do

00:26:32.490 --> 00:26:34.924
is to prevent others
from being trapped.

00:26:35.026 --> 00:26:36.721
We can't abandon our crew.

00:26:36.795 --> 00:26:38.854
If you could delay
your mission...

00:26:38.930 --> 00:26:43.458
My orders are to seal the rift
by this time tomorrow.

00:26:43.535 --> 00:26:47.494
If you want to attempt a rescue
between now and then,

00:26:47.572 --> 00:26:52.532
the risk is yours to take,
but I wouldn't advise it.

00:26:54.212 --> 00:26:55.144
Launch the probe.

00:26:55.213 --> 00:26:56.202
Aye, Captain.

00:26:56.281 --> 00:26:58.272
Work with B'Elanna and Seven
to enhance the sensors.

00:26:58.350 --> 00:26:59.942
Do whatever you can
to find Tom and Tuvok.

00:27:00.018 --> 00:27:01.042
I'll be looking for a way

00:27:01.119 --> 00:27:02.711
to counter
those gravitational forces.

00:27:09.094 --> 00:27:10.061
Come in.

00:27:11.563 --> 00:27:12.894
I've been brushing up

00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:14.898
on sinkholes,
quantum singularities.

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:16.160
Any luck?

00:27:16.234 --> 00:27:18.498
All the data leads me
to the same conclusion.

00:27:18.570 --> 00:27:20.265
They're mono-directional
phenomena...

00:27:20.338 --> 00:27:21.737
what goes in doesn't come out.

00:27:21.806 --> 00:27:23.000
Well, if it's any consolation,

00:27:23.074 --> 00:27:24.701
something's coming out
of that anomaly.

00:27:24.776 --> 00:27:25.708
What is it?

00:27:25.777 --> 00:27:26.903
Telemetry from our probe.

00:27:26.978 --> 00:27:28.878
We've located
the shuttle's distress beacon

00:27:28.947 --> 00:27:30.744
on a Class-D planet.

00:27:30.815 --> 00:27:33.249
Vulcan, human, alien life signs.

00:27:33.318 --> 00:27:35.786
At least we know they're alive.

00:27:35.854 --> 00:27:37.913
Keep reading.

00:27:42.894 --> 00:27:46.295
There's astronomical data here
covering a three-month period.

00:27:46.364 --> 00:27:47.592
How is that possible?

00:27:47.666 --> 00:27:50.533
There seems to be some sort
of temporal differential.

00:27:50.602 --> 00:27:52.263
How big a differential?

00:27:52.337 --> 00:27:53.634
It's difficult to say,

00:27:53.705 --> 00:27:55.798
but every hour
that passes for us

00:27:55.874 --> 00:27:58.900
could mean weeks, even months
for Tom and Tuvok.

00:27:58.977 --> 00:28:01.377
Months trying to survive
in a Class-D environment?

00:28:01.446 --> 00:28:03.414
And more than likely,
they've assumed

00:28:03.481 --> 00:28:05.312
that we left them behind
long ago.

00:28:05.383 --> 00:28:06.645
Ready for the bad news?

00:28:06.718 --> 00:28:07.742
You're kidding.

00:28:07.819 --> 00:28:10.083
The gravitational stress
is increasing.

00:28:10.155 --> 00:28:13.454
Seven believes the sinkhole
is on the verge of collapse.

00:28:13.525 --> 00:28:16.358
When it does, everything inside
will be crushed.

00:28:30.642 --> 00:28:32.610
Noss!

00:28:43.555 --> 00:28:45.682
Medical tricorder.

00:28:47.092 --> 00:28:48.525
We were ambushed.

00:28:48.593 --> 00:28:50.857
Give me 20 milligrams
of inaprovaline.

00:28:50.929 --> 00:28:53.022
They got away with a pair of
resonator coils that we found.

00:28:53.098 --> 00:28:54.258
Three fractured ribs,

00:28:54.332 --> 00:28:57.096
subdural hematoma,
internal bleeding.

00:28:57.168 --> 00:28:58.192
Will he live?

00:28:58.269 --> 00:28:59.497
Vulcans are very resilient.

00:28:59.571 --> 00:29:00.538
He'll be fine.

00:29:03.274 --> 00:29:06.732
How long has it been
since I was last activated?

00:29:06.811 --> 00:29:08.039
Almost two months.

00:29:08.113 --> 00:29:09.603
Two months?!

00:29:12.450 --> 00:29:14.884
So... what's new?

00:29:14.986 --> 00:29:16.510
Oh, same old thing...

00:29:16.588 --> 00:29:19.989
fighting off scavengers,
hunting spiders...

00:29:20.058 --> 00:29:21.753
No word from Voyager?

00:29:21.826 --> 00:29:25.592
They're probably 300 light-years
closer to home by now.

00:29:25.663 --> 00:29:27.893
I think
I should remain on-line

00:29:28.032 --> 00:29:30.626
until Mr. Tuvok
is fully recovered.

00:29:32.837 --> 00:29:35.704
It's good to have you back, Doc.

00:29:51.189 --> 00:29:52.781
Rest.

00:29:54.325 --> 00:29:56.589
How long was I unconscious?

00:29:56.661 --> 00:29:58.720
Too many hours.

00:29:58.797 --> 00:30:01.231
Mr. Paris?

00:30:01.299 --> 00:30:02.425
He'll be fine.

00:30:04.669 --> 00:30:08.571
I was afraid.

00:30:08.640 --> 00:30:11.734
It is good to see your eyes.

00:30:19.083 --> 00:30:20.482
Don't.

00:30:23.688 --> 00:30:28.421
I only want...
to show you how I feel.

00:30:36.801 --> 00:30:41.500
You... you-you feel
nothing for me?

00:30:41.573 --> 00:30:43.268
I told you,

00:30:43.341 --> 00:30:46.640
I don't experience emotion.

00:30:46.711 --> 00:30:52.547
I have developed an appreciation
and respect for you...

00:30:52.617 --> 00:30:54.585
nothing more.

00:31:00.191 --> 00:31:01.590
Nothing?

00:31:02.927 --> 00:31:04.360
I am sorry.

00:31:04.429 --> 00:31:07.262
I cannot return your affection.

00:31:09.667 --> 00:31:11.498
You cannot

00:31:11.569 --> 00:31:13.264
or you will not?

00:31:14.706 --> 00:31:16.139
A minor distinction.

00:31:16.207 --> 00:31:17.572
Logic!

00:31:17.642 --> 00:31:19.075
I hate logic!

00:31:19.143 --> 00:31:23.512
Your emotions will only
exacerbate the situation.

00:31:23.581 --> 00:31:25.071
Shevrot kat!

00:31:25.149 --> 00:31:27.845
Insulting me will not help.

00:31:27.919 --> 00:31:29.682
Derot oraht!

00:31:40.498 --> 00:31:41.965
We can use
the multispatial probe

00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:43.260
as a transporter relay.

00:31:43.334 --> 00:31:44.392
It'll take a little time

00:31:44.469 --> 00:31:46.130
to reconfigure
the targeting scanners,

00:31:46.204 --> 00:31:47.637
but, with a little luck,
it should work.

00:31:47.705 --> 00:31:49.229
Any reason we can't
use the same relay

00:31:49.307 --> 00:31:51.172
to send a com signal?

00:31:51.242 --> 00:31:52.641
I don't see why not.

00:31:52.710 --> 00:31:54.940
Good. Let them know
that help is on the way.

00:31:55.013 --> 00:31:57.004
Captain to the Bridge.

00:32:01.552 --> 00:32:03.315
They've started
ahead of schedule.

00:32:03.388 --> 00:32:04.412
Hail them.

00:32:04.489 --> 00:32:05.421
Yes?

00:32:05.490 --> 00:32:06.616
It was my understanding

00:32:06.691 --> 00:32:08.852
you wouldn't begin
for another six hours.

00:32:08.927 --> 00:32:10.326
We're ready now.

00:32:10.395 --> 00:32:11.362
Well, we're not.

00:32:11.429 --> 00:32:12.919
We need at least
another two hours

00:32:12.997 --> 00:32:14.487
to make a rescue attempt.

00:32:14.565 --> 00:32:15.930
I'm sorry.

00:32:16.067 --> 00:32:18.194
How long
until they seal the rift?

00:32:18.269 --> 00:32:20.601
Approximately 30 minutes.

00:32:20.672 --> 00:32:22.230
Then that's all we've got.

00:32:34.018 --> 00:32:35.451
Tuvok?

00:32:37.855 --> 00:32:39.117
Hey!

00:32:39.190 --> 00:32:41.283
I am meditating, Mr. Paris.

00:32:41.359 --> 00:32:42.951
I don't care.

00:32:43.027 --> 00:32:45.086
I trust there is
an urgent reason

00:32:45.163 --> 00:32:46.926
for your lack of courtesy.

00:32:46.998 --> 00:32:48.966
You're damn right there is.

00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:50.897
What did you say to her?

00:32:50.969 --> 00:32:53.733
Our conversation was private.

00:32:53.805 --> 00:32:57.297
Well, whatever you said,
she's talking about leaving,

00:32:57.375 --> 00:32:58.842
going off by herself,

00:32:58.910 --> 00:33:01.606
because it's too painful
to be around you.

00:33:01.679 --> 00:33:05.581
She is under the influence
of unfettered emotions.

00:33:05.650 --> 00:33:10.713
Well, maybe you're able
to "fetter" your emotions,

00:33:10.788 --> 00:33:12.915
but the rest of us
don't have that luxury.

00:33:12.991 --> 00:33:15.482
She is a living,
breathing woman,

00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:18.085
who, for reasons that
I can't begin to fathom,

00:33:18.162 --> 00:33:20.130
has fallen in love with you.

00:33:20.198 --> 00:33:23.065
Now, if you're incapable
of returning her feelings,

00:33:23.134 --> 00:33:25.125
at least show her
some compassion.

00:33:25.203 --> 00:33:26.568
Try to let her down easy.

00:33:26.637 --> 00:33:30.198
There is no easy way
to recover from infatuation.

00:33:30.274 --> 00:33:31.764
Oh, really?

00:33:31.843 --> 00:33:35.836
And what do you know
about infatuation?

00:33:35.913 --> 00:33:37.881
More than you might imagine.

00:33:37.949 --> 00:33:39.246
Enlighten me.

00:33:39.317 --> 00:33:41.444
I have no intention
of continuing

00:33:41.519 --> 00:33:43.384
this conversation any further.

00:33:43.454 --> 00:33:44.785
Come on, Tuvok.

00:33:44.856 --> 00:33:46.221
Come on!

00:33:46.290 --> 00:33:50.090
It's just you, me and the rocks.

00:33:59.470 --> 00:34:02.667
When I was a young man,
I experienced

00:34:02.740 --> 00:34:06.176
an emotional attraction
toward a woman.

00:34:06.244 --> 00:34:08.269
It nearly destroyed me.

00:34:08.346 --> 00:34:10.610
Your wife?

00:34:10.681 --> 00:34:12.012
No.

00:34:12.083 --> 00:34:16.486
Her name was Jara,
a Terrelian female.

00:34:16.554 --> 00:34:18.283
I would have violated

00:34:18.356 --> 00:34:23.123
every tenet of Vulcan philosophy
simply to be near her.

00:34:24.495 --> 00:34:26.827
She must have
really been something.

00:34:26.898 --> 00:34:30.390
I lost all sense of who I was.

00:34:31.969 --> 00:34:34.062
The emotional attraction
I felt for her

00:34:34.138 --> 00:34:37.505
became a kind of... insanity.

00:34:37.575 --> 00:34:41.875
Tuvok, everyone feels
a little insane

00:34:41.946 --> 00:34:44.608
when they fall in love...

00:34:44.682 --> 00:34:47.207
but it's worth the risk.

00:34:47.285 --> 00:34:49.219
For you, perhaps,

00:34:49.287 --> 00:34:51.380
but I am Vulcan.

00:34:51.456 --> 00:34:55.756
My natural emotions
are erratic, volatile.

00:34:55.827 --> 00:35:00.196
If I don't control them,
they will control me.

00:35:04.268 --> 00:35:06.862
Whatever happened to Jara?

00:35:06.938 --> 00:35:09.099
I chose to leave her.

00:35:09.173 --> 00:35:12.142
I spent several
months in isolation,

00:35:12.210 --> 00:35:14.735
studying with a Vulcan master.

00:35:14.812 --> 00:35:17.747
I learned to suppress
my emotions.

00:35:25.890 --> 00:35:27.187
Too bad.

00:35:33.898 --> 00:35:35.422
Gravimetric distortions.

00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:36.831
What's causing them?

00:35:36.901 --> 00:35:38.095
Unknown.

00:35:49.614 --> 00:35:51.741
No response to our hails,
Captain.

00:35:51.816 --> 00:35:53.374
At this rate,
their anti-graviton beam

00:35:53.451 --> 00:35:56.113
will seal the distortion
in approximately 29 minutes.

00:35:56.187 --> 00:35:57.882
Transporter status?

00:35:57.955 --> 00:35:59.388
I've completed
the reconfiguration,

00:35:59.457 --> 00:36:00.947
but we're only going
to be able to relay

00:36:01.092 --> 00:36:02.684
one transporter beam
through the probe.

00:36:02.760 --> 00:36:04.091
We'll have to get Tom
and Tuvok

00:36:04.162 --> 00:36:06.460
within a two-meter radius
of their distress beacon.

00:36:06.531 --> 00:36:07.657
Harry?

00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:10.624
I've opened a channel.

00:36:10.701 --> 00:36:13.363
Voyager to away team.

00:36:17.475 --> 00:36:18.442
What is it?

00:36:18.509 --> 00:36:19.441
The distress beacon.

00:36:19.510 --> 00:36:20.636
We're receiving a transmission.

00:36:20.711 --> 00:36:23.111
Can you route it through
your com system?

00:36:27.652 --> 00:36:30.143
If I'm right, this message

00:36:30.221 --> 00:36:33.247
was sent almost nine hours ago
on a very slow carrier wave.

00:36:33.324 --> 00:36:35.121
Can you speed it up?

00:36:35.193 --> 00:36:37.093
I'll try.

00:36:37.161 --> 00:36:46.297
Voy-a-ger... to... away team.

00:36:46.370 --> 00:36:49.066
A transporter beam
with a radius of two meters

00:36:49.140 --> 00:36:50.471
will activate
at the coordinates

00:36:50.541 --> 00:36:53.066
of your distress beacon
in exactly 30 minutes.

00:36:53.144 --> 00:36:54.236
"30 minutes"?

00:36:54.312 --> 00:36:56.439
That would have been
over eight hours ago.

00:36:56.514 --> 00:36:57.947
Shh. There's more.

00:36:58.082 --> 00:37:00.642
Be advised we've detected
a temporal differential

00:37:00.718 --> 00:37:02.083
between our two positions.

00:37:02.153 --> 00:37:05.611
According to our calculations,
the differential ratio

00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:08.750
is.4744 seconds per minute.

00:37:08.826 --> 00:37:11.886
Repeat: Voyager to away team.

00:37:11.996 --> 00:37:14.487
A transporter beam
with a radius of two meters...

00:37:14.565 --> 00:37:18.023
According to that formula,
30 minutes would translate

00:37:18.102 --> 00:37:20.536
to two days, 11 hours
and 47 seconds.

00:37:20.605 --> 00:37:22.539
Well, we've waited this long.

00:37:22.607 --> 00:37:24.268
Tom.

00:37:48.499 --> 00:37:50.330
The force field is holding.

00:37:51.769 --> 00:37:53.396
Not for long
if they keep pelting us

00:37:53.471 --> 00:37:54.995
with these photon grenades.

00:37:56.440 --> 00:37:57.771
How are we supposed
to hold them off

00:37:57.842 --> 00:37:58.774
for two more days?

00:38:04.248 --> 00:38:06.876
The rift will be sealed
in less than two minutes.

00:38:06.951 --> 00:38:08.646
Move us into range.

00:38:08.719 --> 00:38:10.812
Stand by for transport.

00:38:10.888 --> 00:38:11.855
Yes, ma'am.

00:38:11.922 --> 00:38:13.446
The force field is losing power.

00:38:13.524 --> 00:38:14.718
Time?

00:38:14.792 --> 00:38:17.283
We still have another
hour before transport.

00:38:18.829 --> 00:38:20.023
Where are you going?

00:38:20.097 --> 00:38:22.531
To repair the field generator.

00:38:22.600 --> 00:38:24.500
I will accompany you.

00:38:24.568 --> 00:38:25.535
No. You stay.

00:38:25.603 --> 00:38:27.366
Prepare for the attack.

00:38:27.438 --> 00:38:29.030
You can't go alone.

00:38:29.106 --> 00:38:32.906
Risking two lives...
would be illogical.

00:38:37.581 --> 00:38:39.742
We're in transporter range.

00:38:39.817 --> 00:38:43.480
Link up with the probe
and relay the signal.

00:38:43.554 --> 00:38:44.748
Stand by.

00:38:44.822 --> 00:38:47.655
I've got a lock on their beacon.

00:38:47.725 --> 00:38:49.886
They're supposed to be ready
for transport in 32 seconds.

00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:51.928
Let's hope
they don't stand us up.

00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:55.124
Begin 20-second countdown
on my mark.

00:38:55.199 --> 00:38:56.689
Now.

00:38:57.935 --> 00:39:00.233
We've got less
than ten minutes to transport.

00:39:00.304 --> 00:39:01.566
Where the hell is Noss?!

00:39:01.639 --> 00:39:03.800
I'll find her.

00:39:18.255 --> 00:39:20.155
15 seconds.

00:39:20.224 --> 00:39:21.316
Fourteen...

00:39:21.392 --> 00:39:22.757
thirteen...

00:39:34.538 --> 00:39:35.562
Tuvok...

00:39:35.639 --> 00:39:38.301
I could not leave you behind.

00:39:43.614 --> 00:39:44.842
Nine...

00:39:44.915 --> 00:39:46.348
eight...

00:39:46.417 --> 00:39:47.782
seven...

00:39:47.852 --> 00:39:49.513
Now, Mr. Paris!

00:40:01.899 --> 00:40:03.526
Hurry.

00:40:06.871 --> 00:40:08.338
Four...

00:40:08.406 --> 00:40:10.340
three...

00:40:10.408 --> 00:40:11.500
two...

00:40:11.575 --> 00:40:13.702
Initialize transport sequence.

00:40:13.778 --> 00:40:15.075
Energize.

00:40:21.919 --> 00:40:23.784
We've got them.

00:40:26.557 --> 00:40:28.184
Welcome back.

00:40:28.259 --> 00:40:29.783
Who?

00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:31.851
A friend.

00:40:38.569 --> 00:40:45.236
Commander Tuvok,
Personal Log, Stardate 52438.9.

00:40:45.309 --> 00:40:47.903
We are en route
to Noss' homeworld.

00:40:47.978 --> 00:40:51.277
As I prepare to say good-bye,
I find myself experiencing

00:40:51.348 --> 00:40:53.213
a certain discomfort.

00:40:53.284 --> 00:40:55.275
Tuvok.

00:40:57.321 --> 00:40:58.982
Weird day.

00:40:59.056 --> 00:41:00.580
Problems?

00:41:00.658 --> 00:41:02.319
I've spent the last two months

00:41:02.393 --> 00:41:04.725
wondering if I'd ever
see B'Elanna again.

00:41:04.795 --> 00:41:08.561
As far as she's concerned,
it's only been two days.

00:41:08.632 --> 00:41:10.930
I guess I expected her
to have missed me, too.

00:41:11.068 --> 00:41:12.933
Were it not
for the time differential,

00:41:13.070 --> 00:41:14.833
I'm sure she would
have experienced

00:41:14.905 --> 00:41:15.929
a deep sense of loss.

00:41:16.073 --> 00:41:18.473
You know something?

00:41:18.542 --> 00:41:19.566
I always thought

00:41:19.643 --> 00:41:21.907
that beneath
that cold Vulcan exterior

00:41:21.979 --> 00:41:26.416
lay a... even colder
Vulcan interior,

00:41:26.484 --> 00:41:30.944
but now, I'm convinced
you're a hopeless romantic.

00:41:31.021 --> 00:41:34.422
There is no need
to insult me, Mr. Paris.

00:41:34.492 --> 00:41:36.460
Oh, here they are now.

00:41:36.527 --> 00:41:39.621
I was just getting Noss' recipe
for sautéed spiders.

00:41:39.697 --> 00:41:42.257
She told me
how much you enjoyed them.

00:41:42.333 --> 00:41:44.961
Let's just say
it's an acquired taste.

00:41:47.171 --> 00:41:48.866
Good-bye, Tom.

00:41:55.179 --> 00:41:56.646
Thank you.

00:42:00.150 --> 00:42:02.914
Come on, Neelix.

00:42:02.987 --> 00:42:03.919
Oh. Of course.

00:42:03.988 --> 00:42:05.012
Crewman.

00:42:13.364 --> 00:42:14.661
I'm sorry.

00:42:14.732 --> 00:42:18.031
For what?

00:42:18.102 --> 00:42:23.506
I know how difficult
this was for you...

00:42:23.574 --> 00:42:27.601
for us.

00:42:27.678 --> 00:42:30.272
I just wish things
had been different.

00:42:30.347 --> 00:42:33.043
As do I.

00:43:04.582 --> 00:43:06.072
I understand.

00:43:09.687 --> 00:43:11.416
Thank you.

00:43:39.416 --> 00:43:42.112
Live long and prosper, Noss.

00:43:44.788 --> 00:43:48.053
You, too.

00:44:19.857 --> 00:44:22.724
Infinite diversity...

00:44:22.793 --> 00:44:26.354
In infinite combinations.

00:44:28.265 --> 00:44:30.790
Your training is now complete.

00:44:30.868 --> 00:44:32.495
You have done well.

00:44:33.570 --> 00:44:35.538
Thank you.

00:44:35.606 --> 00:44:38.666
You are now prepared to return
to the world.

00:44:38.742 --> 00:44:42.143
Grief, anger, fear
and especially love,

00:44:42.212 --> 00:44:45.204
will never threaten you again.

00:44:46.283 --> 00:44:50.276
I am... grateful.
